# Real ballot-level preference data for the 2002 Irish general election, Dublin North
# constituency (12 candidates, 3 seats, 43942 valid votes). Converted from the "soi" (strict
# orders, incomplete) format at https://www.preflib.org/dataset/00001 (PrefLib's "Irish
# Election Data", series 00001-00000001) -- originally posted by the Dublin County Returning
# Officer, since taken offline, and donated to PrefLib by Jeffrey O'Neill (OpenSTV.org).
#
# First preferences match Wikipedia's "Dublin North (Dail constituency)" page exactly: Sargent
# 7294, Ryan 6359, Glennon 5892, Wright 5658, Daly 5501, Kennedy 5253, Owen 4012, Davis 1350,
# Boland 1177, Goulding 914, Quinn 285, Walshe 247 (sums to 43942). Sargent, Ryan, and Glennon
# were the three TDs actually elected -- this file's expected replay (below) reproduces that
# same winner set exactly.
#
# IMPORTANT CAVEAT: real Irish Dail counts historically transfer surplus votes by physically
# resampling a random subset of the parcel at full value, not by a deterministic
# weighted/fractional ratio -- so this is NOT a replay of Dublin North's own official
# count-by-count record (which isn't publicly available at ballot level in any case). The
# expected figures instead come from applying this project's own Droop+WIGM engine (the same
# building blocks as the bundled "scottish" ruleset) to this real ballot data, then
# cross-validating every stage's tallies against jklundell/droop's independent Python
# implementation of that same deterministic method (github.com/jklundell/droop) -- matched
# exactly, to droop's own 5-decimal-place precision, at every single stage.
